"repo": "force-field-fitting", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "319fa7170064c4dd1e40c29066ea877e4ad6d39e", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2025-01-15T17:24:02Z", "repo": "force-field-fitting", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "c3e9ae6078b0b9870de842419b822be6f7ef93ce", "message": "Create co2_configs.py\n\nScript to create various orientations of CO2-CO2 for ab initio calculations. Resulting pair potentials can be used to fit empirical force fields.", "created_at": "2025-01-15T03:38:36Z", "repo": "force-field-fitting", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "9b3e88e40d7dd74b714ebdaea4ed3870f2343a70", "message": "Update generate_configs.py\n\nFixed configs.fit file writing", "created_at": "2024-11-25T22:10:40Z", "repo": "force-field-fitting", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ef68caec7317f9ff5613eaeed09d8b4c564cef2f", "message": "Delete random_dimer.py", "created_at": "2024-11-11T20:28:36Z", "repo": "force-field-fitting", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "6e814f94f402ae1b1d9f4e2134b4ad773b725835", "message": "Delete periodic_dimer.py", "created_at": "2024-11-11T20:28:24Z", "repo": "force-field-fitting", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "879324bae212320560109a156c8fa7f89e9eaf80", "message": "Create README.md", "created_at": "2024-11-11T20:28:11Z", "repo": "force-field-fitting", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "f551cad5dcd0badd6a86dc8533a9bcc1d6db90fe", "message": "Create generate_configs.py\n\nCreates configurations of noble gases with H2 and N2 dimers for force field parameterization. Two force field types available for fitting:\r\n\r\nH2CNO: places a previously mentioned gas on a target atomic index and increments the distance in a straight line\r\n\r\nAA: places a previously mentioned gas randomly around the molecular structure within 0.75-1.5 times the vdW radii of the structure\r\n\r\nWritten specifically for MOFs, but will work with other structures as well.", "created_at": "2024-11-11T20:28:00Z", "repo": "force-field-fitting", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "a0801964be0e3834347f54fb676f347c601a817c", "message": "Upload periodic_dimer.py\n\nPython script that places a guest molecule within 0.75x to 1.5x the van der Waal radii of the atoms in a periodic structure. 3D random rotations of dimers (H2, N2, etc.) are handled by quaternions. Also creates input scripts for CP2K.", "created_at": "2024-08-30T22:49:29Z", "repo": "force-field-fitting", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4f43255fe79146b6f5f277a8397395eedc770025", "message": "File uploaded\n\nA python script that creates xyz files for a guest molecule moving away from the center of mass to an atom in the input structure. For dimer gases (H2, N2, etc.), 3D random rotations are calculated with quaternions. Used for fitting force field parameters to ab initio energies.", "created_at": "2024-08-30T22:24:41Z", "repo": "force-field-fitting", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}], "prs": []}